 "text": "The most famous psychology experiment was partly staged. 1971, Stanford. Funded by the U.S. Navy, college students played guards and prisoners in a fake prison. The guards turned cruel, stopped after six days. The lesson? Put good people in a bad role and they turn evil. But later recordings showed staff coaching the guards to be tough. And one famous breakdown? The prisoner said he faked it. Here's the trick. Tell people what you expect, and they'll give it to you. Follow for more dark psychology.",
